From 00bda2c631736949bdd12f39e57167859db540c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:18:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dc target: do not split functions at targets decoded from
 data sections

The main-EXE split pre-pass scanned data-section CFGs and minted an entry
for every word that decoded as a branch. With --target dc those CFGs are
skipped. Xenogears: 792 -> 15 split entries, SH-4 code 3.34 -> 2.12 MB
(2.03 -> 1.04 MB with DC_GUEST_RAM_MMU). PC output is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011whdg2yDfX3EoxgBeZLS6B
